#: ../../_static/plots/C4_solar_system_simulation_visualization.py:18
#: ../../_static/plots/C4_solar_system_simulation_visualization.py:28
msgid ""
"Real-time solar system simulation demonstration showing solar generation,"
" battery operation, system connection states, and utility grid exchange "
"during controlled operational scenarios"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C4_rsgp_solar_system_simulation.rst:188
msgid ""
"Along the data from NSRDB, the logged CSV files provide all the data "
"needed to carry out analysis on the trends of power generation and "
"consumption. Trend analysis might lead to improvements on the power "
"management solutions. Additionally, AI techniques can be used to benefit "
"from the data and extend the power manager with AI capabilities. This "
"could be especially useful to predict shortages of power generation and "
"thus switch the operation mode of the inverter to import from utility to "
"keep the battery for that shortage and thus maintain long-term system "
"stability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:4
msgid "Power Management"
msgstr "إدارة الطاقة"

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:7
msgid ""
"The power management system serves as the intelligent coordination layer."
" This chapter examines the algorithms and mathematical foundation that "
"enable the power manager to achieve efficient energy utilization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:9
msgid ""
"The power manager implements an adaptive algorithm that learns from the "
"consumption patterns and adjusts distribution weights as to minimize "
"utility grid dependence. The system operates through two primary "
"components: the central ``PowerManager`` that coordinates system-wide "
"decisions, and individual ``VirtualBattery`` instances that represent "
"each house's allocation within the shared battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:12
msgid "System Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:13
msgid ""
"The power management system integrates with both the houses simulation "
"and solar system simulation through well-defined interfaces that enable "
"real-time coordination and control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:19
msgid ""
"The power manager operates on a configurable update cycle, typically set "
"to match the houses simulation update interval of 100 milliseconds. "
"During each update cycle, the manager executes a sequence of coordinated "
"algorithms that process current system state, update virtual battery "
"parameters, and make power distribution decisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:21
msgid ""
"The coordination interface provides bidirectional communication between "
"components. The houses simulation provides current load demands and "
"accepts load line control commands. The solar system simulation provides "
"generation data, battery state information, and accepts load requirements"
" while returning actual power delivery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:24
msgid "Virtual Battery System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:25
msgid ""
"The virtual battery system partitions the shared physical battery among "
"individual houses based on their consumption patterns. Each house "
"receives a dedicated ``VirtualBattery`` instance that tracks its "
"allocated capacity, manages charge and discharge, and tracks the house's "
"weight that determines its share of the total system capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:28
msgid "Mathematical Foundation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:29
msgid ""
"The virtual battery allocation system employs several mathematical "
"relationships to ensure fair and efficient energy distribution. The "
"fundamental relationship establishes the connection between virtual "
"battery capacity and system-wide resources:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:31
msgid "C_{vb,i} = \\frac {C_{total}}{N} \\times w_i"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:35
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:59
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:73
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:139
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:221
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:289
#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:310
msgid "where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:37
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`C_{vb,i}` represents the total capacity of the i-th virtual battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:39
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`C_{total}` represents the total capacity of the physical battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:41
msgid "`N` represents the number of houses in the system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:43
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`w_{i}` represents the weight assigned to the i-th house"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:45
msgid ""
"The weight constraint ensures that the sum of all virtual capacities "
"equals the total physical capacity:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:47
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\sum_{i=1}^{N} w_{i} = N"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:51
msgid ""
"where *N* represents the number of houses in the system. This constraint "
"ensures energy conservation between the physical battery and the virtual "
"batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:53
msgid ""
"The system implements weight boundaries to ensure fairness and prevent "
"extreme allocations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:55
#, python-brace-format
msgid "w_{min} \\leq w_i \\leq w_{max}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:61
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`w_{min} = \\alpha` (guaranteed minimum weight, typically 0.8)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:63
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`w_{max} = 1 + (1 - \\alpha) \\times (N - 1)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:66
msgid "Virtual Battery Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:67
msgid ""
"The virtual battery implements charge and discharge operations that "
"maintain energy conservation across the distributed system. The charge "
"operation accounts for charging efficiency and capacity constraints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:69
msgid ""
"P_{charge,actual} = \\min\\left(P_{charge} \\times \\eta_{charge} \\times"
" \\Delta t, C_{total} - C_{residual}\\right) \\times \\frac{1}{\\Delta t "
"\\times \\eta_{charge}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:75
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`P_{charge,actual}` represents the actual power consumed for charging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:76
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`P_{charge}` represents the requested charging power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:77
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`\\eta_{charge}` represents the charging efficiency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:78
msgid ""
"`\\Delta t` represents the time interval in hours: `\\Delta t = "
"\\frac{\\Delta t_{s}}{3600}` where `\\Delta t_{s}` represents the time "
"interval in seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:79
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`C_{total}` represents the maximum capacity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:80
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`C_{residual}` represents the current residual capacity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:82
msgid ""
"The discharge operation implements efficiency losses and capacity "
"limitations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:84
msgid ""
"P_{discharge,actual} = \\min\\left(\\frac{P_{discharge} \\times \\Delta "
"t}{\\eta_{charge}}, C_{residual}\\right) \\times "
"\\frac{\\eta_{charge}}{\\Delta t}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:88
msgid "The energy conversion between power and capacity uses the relationship:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:90
msgid "E = P \\times \\Delta t"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:94
msgid "where energy is measured in watt-hours and power in watts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:97
msgid "Weight Adjustment Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:98
msgid ""
"The adjustment function modifies weights while maintaining system "
"constraints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:100
#, python-brace-format
msgid "w_{i}^{t+1} = \\text{clamp}(w_{i}^{t} + \\Delta w_{i}, w_{min}, w_{max})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:104
msgid ""
"After adjusting the weights, the new capacity for the virtual battery is "
"calculated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:106
msgid "C_{vb,i}^{t+1} = \\frac {C_{total}}{N} \\times w_{i}^{t+1}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:110
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When weight adjustment reduces total capacity `C_{vb,i}^{t+1}` below "
"current residual capacity `C_{vb,i}^{residual}`, the excess energy is "
"calculated and returned to the system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:112
#, python-brace-format
msgid "E_{excess} = \\max(0, C_{vb,i}^{residual} - C_{vb,i}^{t+1})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:116
msgid ""
"This excess energy is then redistributed among the other virtual "
"batteries to conserve the energy during system optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../_static/plots/C5_virtual_battery_weight_and_allocation.py:7
msgid ""
"(:download:`Source code "
"<../_build/gettext/plot_directive/_static/plots/C5_virtual_battery_weight_and_allocation.py>`,"
" :download:`png "
"<../_build/gettext/plot_directive/_static/plots/C5_virtual_battery_weight_and_allocation.png>`,"
" :download:`hires.png "
