#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:282
msgid "System-Wide Load Line Coordination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:283
msgid ""
"The power manager coordinates load line states between individual houses "
"and the solar system inverter. When the inverter implements load shedding"
" due to extreme power shortage, the power manager propagates this state "
"to all connected houses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:285
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\neg LL_{inverter} \\rightarrow \\neg LL_{i}, \\quad \\forall i"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:291
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`LL_{inverter}` represents the state of the inverter load line connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:292
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`LL_{i}` represents the state of the load line connection of the i-th "
"house"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:294
msgid ""
"This ensures individual house load line states remain consistent with "
"overall system capacity and prevents conflicts between local and system-"
"wide load management decisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:296
msgid ""
"Restoration operates automatically after a configurable set interval "
"(typically 30 seconds)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:299
msgid "Utility Power Export Distribution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:300
msgid ""
"The power management system implements an algorithm for distributing "
"utility export power among houses when excess energy becomes available "
"for grid export. The algorithm ensures fair distribution of export "
"benefits while accounting for individual house contributions to system "
"efficiency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:303
msgid "Export Eligibility and Weight Calculation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:304
msgid ""
"The utility export distribution algorithm operates exclusively on houses "
"that maintain active utility line connections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:306
msgid "S_{export} = \\{i \\mid UL_{i} \\}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:312
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`UL_{i}` represents the utility line connection state of the i-th house"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:314
msgid ""
"The export weight calculation employs inverse virtual battery weights to "
"provide higher export allocation to houses with lower virtual battery "
"weights, creating incentives for efficient energy usage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:316
msgid "w_{export,i} = \\frac{1}{w_{vb,i}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:320
msgid ""
"The normalized export distribution calculates each house's share of total"
" export power using sum normalization:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:322
msgid ""
"w_{export,norm,i} = \\frac{w_{export,i}}{\\sum_{j \\in S_{export}} "
"w_{export,j}}, \\quad \\forall i \\in S_{export}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:327
msgid "Export Power Allocation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:328
msgid "The final export power allocation for each eligible house follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:330
#, python-brace-format
msgid "P_{export,i} = P_{export,total} \\times w_{export,norm,i}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:334
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where `P_{export,total}` represents the total power available for utility"
" export from the solar system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/C5_rsgp_power_management.rst:336
msgid ""
"This ensures that houses with more efficient virtual battery utilization "
"(lower weights) receive proportionally higher export benefits, creating "
"economic incentives for optimal energy usage."
msgstr ""

